5. Methodology
5.1 Dataset
The IMDB Large Movie Review Dataset contains 50,000 movie reviews evenly split between 25,000 positive and 25,000 negative examples. The dataset is perfectly balanced, eliminating the need for class weighting.
5.2 Data Splitting
•	Training set: 40,000 reviews (80%)
•	Validation set: 5,000 reviews (10%) — used for hyperparameter tuning
•	Test set: 5,000 reviews (10%) — used exclusively for final evaluation
5.3 Preprocessing Steps
•	HTML tag removal: Regular expressions strip all <br />, <b>, and other HTML elements
•	Special character removal: Non-alphabetic characters replaced with spaces
•	Case normalization: All text converted to lowercase
•	Whitespace normalization: Multiple spaces collapsed to single spaces
•	Sequence padding/truncation: All sequences fixed to 256 tokens
5.4 Training Configuration
Both models were trained using the AdamW optimizer with weight decay of 1e-4. A Cosine Annealing learning rate scheduler gradually reduces the learning rate. Gradient clipping with maximum norm of 1.0 was applied. Bi-LSTM was trained for 5 epochs with learning rate 1e-3 and batch size 32. DistilBERT was fine-tuned for 3 epochs with learning rate 2e-5 and batch size 16.
